WEBVTT

01:47.975 --> 01:50.216
Them flies are getting thick.

01:51.244 --> 01:53.884
Somebody ought to give you a good hosing.

01:53.947 --> 01:54.948
Hmm.

01:55.048 --> 01:56.959
Heat ain't helping.

01:57.718 --> 02:00.324
Well, reckon you'll keep another day.

02:02.322 --> 02:05.633
Be good, I'll bring you
some more water around noon.

02:07.394 --> 02:09.237
Bye, Daddy.

02:34.621 --> 02:37.500
Okay. Come on.

02:39.359 --> 02:40.429
Come.

02:41.161 --> 02:42.868
What the devil is all this about?

02:42.963 --> 02:44.874
Why was I brought here?

02:45.932 --> 02:48.208
Games? Must we?

02:49.369 --> 02:51.713
Not that I mind a slight case of abduction,

02:51.805 --> 02:54.285
but I have tickets for the
theater this evening;.

02:54.341 --> 02:56.116
To a show I was looking forward m.

02:56.176 --> 02:58.850
And I get, well, kind of unreasonable
about things like that.

02:58.945 --> 03:02.358
With such expert play-acting,
you make this very room a theater.

03:02.449 --> 03:04.224
You have a good walk?

03:06.153 --> 03:07.632
Yes, my dear.

03:08.188 --> 03:10.134
Top notch walk this morning.

03:12.459 --> 03:14.803
Top notch constitutional.

03:20.133 --> 03:22.807
It's been weeks since I left my mark.

03:23.203 --> 03:25.513
Would that they had eyes 10 see.

03:26.339 --> 03:29.013
Hey! Don't you get Miss Billy in here
with them dirty feet!

03:37.818 --> 03:39.388
Sorry, old chap.

03:57.204 --> 03:59.844
You wanna make flowers today?

04:02.409 --> 04:03.683
I'm busy.

04:04.211 --> 04:06.623
I have very important work to do.

04:07.380 --> 04:08.518
M'!

04:09.683 --> 04:12.960
Ascension removes me
from the disk and the loop.

04:13.854 --> 04:15.697
I'm near final stage.

04:16.890 --> 04:18.528
Some mornings,

04:19.025 --> 04:21.301
I can see the infernal plane.

04:22.763 --> 04:26.142
You haven't made flowers on me
for maybe three weeks.

04:26.767 --> 04:28.644
Makes me sad, is all.

04:31.204 --> 04:35.311
Ah! Come up on me lap, lass. Here.

04:35.408 --> 04:38.617
And let me comfort you in your distress.

04:38.712 --> 04:41.556
You're gonna make fun
of me again.

04:41.615 --> 04:44.425
Now, why would I do
a thing like that, huh?

04:44.484 --> 04:47.397
Is it because you're nay so bright?

04:47.888 --> 04:50.767
Because of your head
being so slow and like?

04:51.925 --> 04:55.395
Oh, you better let me go,
'cause I'll burn your eggs.

04:56.630 --> 04:57.734
Hmm?

05:06.139 --> 05:08.949
Can you tell me about Grandpa?

05:15.081 --> 05:16.253
Ah!

05:20.520 --> 05:21.692
Mmm.

05:22.923 --> 05:24.925
I was in the cane fields.

05:26.593 --> 05:29.005
And he caught me when I was alone.

05:29.963 --> 05:32.705
And the dirt was warm.

05:33.366 --> 05:35.937
I felt the dirt warm on my back.

05:56.556 --> 05:59.127
You're gonna lose a kneecap
if I gotta ask you again.

05:59.192 --> 06:02.469
Now take it out of the bag
and put it in the machine.

06:24.517 --> 06:25.655
Don't look at me.

06:26.386 --> 06:27.729
Look at the TV.

06:46.339 --> 06:48.683
Oh, Jesus Christ.

06:49.509 --> 06:51.682
Why are you showing me this?

07:02.622 --> 07:05.967
That little girl is the one
you said went to see her daddy,

07:06.059 --> 07:08.539
Marie Fontenot, circa 1990.

07:12.532 --> 07:15.877
I took a "missing juvenile" report.

07:18.071 --> 07:20.551
And when I went back to follow up on it

07:21.274 --> 07:24.312
the file said, "Report made in error."

07:25.545 --> 07:27.252
I never wrote that.

07:28.548 --> 07:31.791
So I marched it right into
the Sheriff, Ted Childress.

07:31.885 --> 07:33.387
He's dead now.

07:33.620 --> 07:34.724
He did it.

07:35.922 --> 07:37.595
What did Sheriff say?

07:37.657 --> 07:39.159
He said he'd changed it.

07:39.893 --> 07:41.964
That he knew the mother and the father.

07:42.062 --> 07:43.939
The aunt and the uncle.

07:44.798 --> 07:47.335
It was a niece once removed from him
or something.

07:48.568 --> 07:51.913
It was a chain of command.
No reason to change it.

07:52.305 --> 07:56.014
I just follow what the big man says.

07:56.643 --> 07:57.849
It's

07:59.279 --> 08:01.020
how this all works.

08:01.481 --> 08:03.984
I tried to get back
with the mother,

08:04.751 --> 08:06.025
I tried to get back with her,

08:06.119 --> 08:08.099
she was gone, she split.

08:08.154 --> 08:09.827
The file was gone.

08:10.290 --> 08:11.598
Nobody said a word.

08:11.658 --> 08:15.834
Later that year, I was in state CID
on Ted's recommendation.

08:15.929 --> 08:18.967
Nobody ever gave me a reason
to second-guess it.

08:19.032 --> 08:20.943
It's chain of command.

08:22.969 --> 08:24.141
Right?

08:27.107 --> 08:28.450
What do you think?

08:29.709 --> 08:31.711
I don't think he's lying.

08:33.613 --> 08:35.320
As far as he knows.

08:35.682 --> 08:37.355
"As far as I know?"

08:37.450 --> 08:39.794
What the fuck is with you, man?

08:40.220 --> 08:43.326
It'll be a whole lot safer
if we staged something, Marty.

08:44.557 --> 08:46.537
Send the Maserati over the guard rail.

09:02.675 --> 09:04.484
Boys, slow down.

09:10.350 --> 09:12.159
Be careful out there.

09:24.097 --> 09:27.169
I can get you a cafeteria lunch
if you're hungry.

09:27.700 --> 09:31.170
That's all right, Miss.
I gotta get on with my work.

09:32.005 --> 09:33.507
Lots to do today.

09:33.573 --> 09:34.574
Oh, all right.

09:59.532 --> 10:01.478
We're gonna hang on
to your phone

10:01.568 --> 10:03.275
and your gun till we get safe.

10:03.369 --> 10:05.406
We'll mail them to you once we know we are.

10:05.472 --> 10:06.974
Does that work for you, Steve?

10:07.073 --> 10:09.417
You can bet your ass it doesn't.

10:09.943 --> 10:12.446
And it's Sheriff Geraci to you, shitheel.

10:12.545 --> 10:16.049
Look, Steve, you're gonna wanna
swing some dick on this thing.

10:16.116 --> 10:18.756
I'm gonna give you
a couple reasons why you won't.

10:18.818 --> 10:21.321
First off, we found this tape
in your possession.

10:21.421 --> 10:24.630
It's a video of the little girl
that you said was not missing.

10:24.724 --> 10:27.796
Second off, all findings
are with lawyers ready to be fonuarded

10:27.894 --> 10:32.400
to media outlets, Feds, CID, US Attorneys.

10:32.465 --> 10:34.945
Should either one of us
get sworn a warrant,

10:35.001 --> 10:37.521
or either one of us just fall off
the face of the fucking Earth,

10:37.570 --> 10:39.777
as people are want to do
in your neck of the woods.

10:39.839 --> 10:42.251
So, just think about
that little girl, Steve.

10:46.779 --> 10:48.588
What about your boat?

10:50.850 --> 10:52.591
That ain't my boat.

10:52.652 --> 10:55.792
- You know whose boat that is?
- I've never seen it before.

10:55.855 --> 10:58.665
It's gonna come back on you, you assholes.

10:59.092 --> 11:00.799
One way or another.

11:00.860 --> 11:02.498
You just think about
that little girl, Steve.

11:02.595 --> 11:05.701
For quite some time,
I'm gonna be thinking about you, Rust.

11:05.798 --> 11:07.675
Hey, one other thing, Steve.

11:07.767 --> 11:11.613
I got an old sniper pal, all right.
Contract's already been paid.

11:12.338 --> 11:14.340
Me or Marty, we see cuffs or coffins,

11:14.440 --> 11:16.351
you're gonna end up in the dirt.

11:16.442 --> 11:18.217
Then we're gonna smear your name.

11:19.312 --> 11:21.519
I got something coming for you, baby.

11:21.614 --> 11:24.151
Your psycho bit don't cut me, boy.

11:25.151 --> 11:26.562
You hear me?

11:33.993 --> 11:35.404
What the fuck? Hey!

11:44.904 --> 11:48.147
I strike you
as more of a talker or a doer, Steve?

11:48.508 --> 11:50.215
That's my fucking car!

11:50.310 --> 11:51.584
God damn it!

11:51.678 --> 11:53.521
L'chaim, fat-ass.

11:54.847 --> 11:56.520
You motherfuckers!

11:57.550 --> 11:58.824
Fuck you!

12:07.660 --> 12:09.105
That's old Sheriff Childress.

12:09.195 --> 12:12.039
He's got no kids.
No location on any of his relatives.

12:14.167 --> 12:16.169
You think they could
have wiped out birth records?

12:16.236 --> 12:17.681
I don't see why not.

12:17.737 --> 12:20.775
I mean, half those hospitals
along the mast are gone now.

12:22.508 --> 12:23.782
You know,

12:24.010 --> 12:27.287
we got a dead end on the relations

12:27.580 --> 12:29.560
then what else is there?

12:29.716 --> 12:30.922
Case files.

12:31.584 --> 12:33.564
You want pre-'98 or after?

12:34.854 --> 12:36.026
After.

12:38.091 --> 12:41.011
We're going to have to be looking
at these records with fresh eyes, Marty.

12:41.194 --> 12:43.697
All right? Like we're totally green.

13:02.315 --> 13:03.885
Why green ears?

13:05.918 --> 13:08.057
I mean, assuming that's our guy.

13:09.589 --> 13:11.262
I don't know exactly.

13:11.324 --> 13:14.794
My thinking was
it was probably leaves of some kind.

13:15.094 --> 13:18.234
You know, 'cause we do know
that he came at her through the woods.

13:27.273 --> 13:28.684
Why? What are you thinking?

13:29.075 --> 13:34.923
I'm looking for '95 Dora Lange
canvassing photos from Erath.

13:35.315 --> 13:36.419
Why?

13:37.850 --> 13:39.090
Well...

13:58.504 --> 13:59.710
Rush

14:00.473 --> 14:02.009
come over here.

14:05.144 --> 14:07.454
Now, you think, back then...

14:08.381 --> 14:12.329
Does that look like a
fresh paint job to you?

14:18.791 --> 14:21.067
- Green ears.
- Yeah.

14:21.661 --> 14:24.232
Maybe they were sticking out of his hat.

14:24.330 --> 14:26.469
Maybe he painted that house.

14:32.472 --> 14:35.009
I'm going to look up old addressees.

14:42.315 --> 14:43.817
Fuck you, man.

14:57.563 --> 15:00.442
Something has been bugging me
for the last 10 years.

15:00.533 --> 15:03.173
Not every day, just now and then.

15:04.337 --> 15:06.840
When we went at it' the day you quit,

15:08.608 --> 15:10.349
were you holding back?

15:10.843 --> 15:13.187
No, I don't see how I could have.

15:14.280 --> 15:15.782
Oh, yeah, you do.

15:15.948 --> 15:20.863
You've always had such
an inﬂated idea of yourself.

15:21.220 --> 15:22.528
Meaning what?

15:22.622 --> 15:25.603
Meaning, it seems pretty damn arrogant

15:25.691 --> 15:28.695
to hold back in a fight with me.

15:30.897 --> 15:33.377
You think you could've put me down?

15:34.534 --> 15:37.777
Ah, I don't know. Hell,
I'd have had to kill you.

15:37.870 --> 15:40.043
And you were so goddamn mad.

15:42.909 --> 15:44.479
Yeah, um...

15:46.045 --> 15:48.548
You know,
when she told me, she said

15:49.549 --> 15:51.153
not to blame you,

15:51.451 --> 15:54.227
that it wasn't your choice' you were drunk

15:55.221 --> 15:57.098
and she made it happen.

15:57.490 --> 15:59.834
Everybody's got a choice, Marty.

16:00.760 --> 16:02.330
Shit, I sure blamed you.

16:02.428 --> 16:04.339
Blamed me for what?

16:05.064 --> 16:09.342
For pushing a good woman
to the point where she had to use me,

16:09.836 --> 16:12.476
use our partnership to get rid of you.

16:13.072 --> 16:15.814
You were just being a lying sack of shit.

16:17.577 --> 16:20.786
You know, she couldn't have used you
if you didn't want some.

16:20.947 --> 16:22.426
There you go.

16:23.082 --> 16:25.084
Everybody's got a choice.

16:28.087 --> 16:30.624
And yet, she still cares about you.

16:32.024 --> 16:34.334
You went to see her, I take it.

16:34.760 --> 16:36.831
- She came by the bar.
What?

16:37.163 --> 16:38.164
When?

16:38.264 --> 16:39.937
She was just checking on you,

16:39.999 --> 16:42.605
wanted to make sure
I wasn't getting you in any trouble.

16:42.668 --> 16:44.944
You should've fucking told me.

16:45.438 --> 16:47.384
Maybe. I guess.

16:49.609 --> 16:51.987
I reckoned it was best
to just avoid her name.

16:52.044 --> 16:55.321
Didn't want to invite judgment.
You never liked being judged.

16:55.381 --> 16:57.827
No, you're right. I don't. Not by you.

16:57.884 --> 16:59.522
Well, I didn't say a word.

16:59.619 --> 17:01.963
Well, I could read it all over your face.

17:02.021 --> 17:05.559
Well, then your problem
is with your face, not mine.

17:09.462 --> 17:12.306
It's hard to find something in a man

17:12.365 --> 17:15.369
who rejects people as much
as you do, you know that?

17:15.468 --> 17:18.574
I never told you how to
live your life, Marty.

17:18.671 --> 17:20.810
No, no, no. You just sat in judgment.

17:20.873 --> 17:22.352
Look, as sentient meat,

17:22.408 --> 17:25.878
however illusory our identities are,

17:25.978 --> 17:29.323
we craft those identities
by making value judgments.

17:29.382 --> 17:31.692
Everybody judges, all the time.

17:32.552 --> 17:34.725
Now, if you got a problem with that,

17:34.820 --> 17:36.424
you're living wrong.

17:41.394 --> 17:43.169
What's scented meat?

18:04.850 --> 18:06.386
Can I help you?

18:07.887 --> 18:09.628
Did you happen
to live here back in '95?

18:09.722 --> 18:11.895
No, we didn't live here back then.

18:11.958 --> 18:13.519
- This is my grandma's place.
- Mmm-hmm.

18:13.960 --> 18:15.439
Your grandma, is she still with us?

18:15.528 --> 18:17.201
- Alive you mean?
- Yeah.

18:17.263 --> 18:20.870
Yeah, she's in an old
folks' place, Abbeville.

18:24.437 --> 18:27.543
Mrs. Hill, now,
this is a very strange question,

18:29.575 --> 18:33.751
but do you remember
back in the winter of '94, '95,

18:34.213 --> 18:36.591
did you get your house painted?

18:38.384 --> 18:40.227
I did. Yes, I did.

18:41.120 --> 18:42.599
A nice green.

18:42.655 --> 18:45.465
I don't remember what they call it anymore.

18:45.558 --> 18:49.301
Do you happen to remember
who it was that painted your house?

18:49.395 --> 18:51.068
Well, yes.

18:51.130 --> 18:54.805
I don't remember the name
but they were nice men.

18:54.900 --> 18:58.177
They worked for our parish,
yard work, house painting.

18:58.270 --> 19:00.944
My church, they got a discount.

19:01.007 --> 19:03.783
- Good work for fair pay, back then.
- Mmm.

19:03.843 --> 19:06.084
Do you remember, by any chance,

19:06.679 --> 19:09.922
names or just any other details?

19:10.149 --> 19:11.253
Um...

19:13.085 --> 19:18.000
I remember they charged $250
for the whole house exterior.

19:19.191 --> 19:21.933
- Hmm.
- And one of the men, the younger one,

19:23.362 --> 19:27.504
he had scarring
all along the bottom of his face.

19:27.600 --> 19:28.840
Mmm-hmm.

19:28.934 --> 19:33.007
Ms. Lily, back then,
did you or your husband work?

19:33.105 --> 19:36.018
My husband, Butch, he's always worked.

19:36.475 --> 19:38.955
He was offshore for city services.

19:39.779 --> 19:41.725
- Did he pay his taxes?
- Always.

19:41.814 --> 19:43.521
A lot of good it did him.

19:43.949 --> 19:46.361
Thank you so much.
You've been really helpful.

19:46.452 --> 19:47.624
Thank you.

19:49.955 --> 19:51.195
There you go.

19:51.290 --> 19:54.203
Husband took the write-off December '94.

19:54.293 --> 19:56.000
$265.

19:56.062 --> 19:59.043
Paid by Butch Hill
to Childress and Son Maintenance.

19:59.131 --> 20:00.166
Mmm-hmm.

20:00.232 --> 20:01.506
Yes. Yes.

20:01.567 --> 20:02.567
Here we go.

20:02.635 --> 20:08.051
Business license first issued
to Billy Childress 1978.

20:08.140 --> 20:10.643
- Same name as that... Yeah.
Sheriff.

20:10.710 --> 20:11.711
Uh...

20:11.811 --> 20:16.726
Okay, business license
not renewed since 2004.

20:20.653 --> 20:23.998
Okay, name comes up a
lot in public records.

20:24.323 --> 20:27.327
Looks like they had a lot
of parish contracts,

20:28.327 --> 20:30.933
public state property, landscapes...

20:31.030 --> 20:32.907
I want to know where he was.

20:32.998 --> 20:34.068
Okay

20:37.036 --> 20:38.743
All over the coast.

20:38.838 --> 20:39.942
Okay.

20:40.506 --> 20:45.182
It looks like they did maintenance
for a lot of schools,

20:45.678 --> 20:48.090
playgrounds, cemeteries.

20:48.180 --> 20:50.524
Run a background on Billy Childress,
find his son.

20:50.583 --> 20:52.187
Okay

20:53.052 --> 20:54.292
Here we go.

20:54.386 --> 20:56.024
William Lee Childress,

20:56.088 --> 20:59.968
born to Lizbeth Childress, 1944, Erath.

21:01.393 --> 21:05.364
No son showing. Address, DMV, old license.

21:05.931 --> 21:08.411
Highway 27, scum.

21:24.383 --> 21:25.487
Get out of here!

21:26.252 --> 21:27.754
Oh! Oh!

21:29.421 --> 21:32.095
Can you smell the flowers,
Miss Billy?

21:32.158 --> 21:35.002
One to the Feds, one to state CID,

21:35.094 --> 21:37.836
one to state attorney, one to US attorney.

21:37.930 --> 21:40.934
Two to national papers,
two to local papers,

21:41.000 --> 21:42.673
two to national channels.

21:43.135 --> 21:46.344
It's a whole story, near as we got it.

21:47.606 --> 21:49.608
There's a copy of the tape in each one.

21:50.009 --> 21:52.455
The case files and our depositions,

21:53.112 --> 21:54.682
everything we got.

21:55.481 --> 21:59.258
Now, 24 hours passes and I don't stop you,

22:00.019 --> 22:01.692
mail them all out.

22:04.456 --> 22:06.265
Then lay low a while.

22:14.099 --> 22:17.205
How's that case going?
Uh, Lake Charles.

22:17.937 --> 22:20.144
None of your fucking business.

22:20.306 --> 22:22.616
Your old partner give you anything yet?

22:22.675 --> 22:24.951
None of your fucking business.

22:25.344 --> 22:26.482
Why did you call me?

22:26.545 --> 22:28.286
Why not my partner?

22:30.182 --> 22:32.355
You I can read, him I can't.

22:32.451 --> 22:34.192
And why would you need to do that?

22:34.687 --> 22:36.689
What have you two been doing?

22:36.789 --> 22:40.236
All those late nights
at your offices the last month?

22:41.794 --> 22:44.798
Christ. So, that's it? That's all you got'?

22:44.864 --> 22:46.207
Ain't for you to know.

22:46.298 --> 22:49.404
But I know you've been pulling case files
all over south Louisiana.

22:50.302 --> 22:52.839
It's about Cohle's theory, way back?

22:52.905 --> 22:54.816
He's fucking with you.

22:55.074 --> 22:57.486
He's a manipulator. Sociopath.

22:57.810 --> 22:59.653
You know this.

23:02.314 --> 23:04.726
What do you know about Sam Tuttle?

23:04.817 --> 23:07.093
All the branches of the family?

23:07.553 --> 23:12.593
The, uh, marsh cove, devil worship,
child sacrifices?

23:13.692 --> 23:15.501
You sound like Cohle.

23:16.195 --> 23:18.368
It points in every direction but him, huh?

23:18.430 --> 23:19.568
Man, I knew you were gonna say that.

23:19.665 --> 23:21.611
You know something' you're obstructing.

23:21.700 --> 23:23.543
We don't know.

23:23.602 --> 23:27.106
But we're following up an idea.
Maybe nothing.

23:27.206 --> 23:28.879
But, time comes,

23:29.675 --> 23:31.848
we know we got something,

23:32.278 --> 23:35.020
you get a call' you gonna
do the right thing?

23:35.581 --> 23:38.255
You're speaking riddles to me, white man.

23:38.350 --> 23:39.556
You sound like Cohle.

23:39.618 --> 23:40.619
Again.

23:40.719 --> 23:45.099
We get something, do you want the call
or you want it to go to someone else?

23:47.459 --> 23:49.097
Give it to me.

23:54.099 --> 23:56.875
Just make sure you come running.

24:36.575 --> 24:37.918
That taste.

24:42.982 --> 24:44.086
What?

24:44.950 --> 24:47.590
Aluminum. Ash.

24:49.421 --> 24:51.298
I've tasted it before.

24:55.861 --> 24:57.932
You still see things ever?

24:58.831 --> 25:00.936
It never stops, not really.

25:01.600 --> 25:05.480
What happened to my head
is not something that gets better.

25:10.542 --> 25:12.681
Uh, this is it.

25:55.687 --> 25:57.223
Call Papania.

25:57.656 --> 25:59.727
Shit. I can't get a signal.

26:01.427 --> 26:03.236
I'm gonna ask to use the phone.

26:06.265 --> 26:07.710
You know what, I'll go ask.

26:10.335 --> 26:11.507
Marty.

26:13.939 --> 26:15.612
This is the place.

26:44.803 --> 26:45.975
Hello.

26:47.906 --> 26:49.476
Aw, damn it!

26:51.110 --> 26:54.455
Oh, pardon me, ma'am,
uh, we're professional surveyors,

26:54.546 --> 26:57.823
and got lost on these back roads
like a couple of greenhorns.

26:58.217 --> 26:59.218
Uh...

26:59.284 --> 27:01.457
Cell phone is getting no service out here.

27:01.553 --> 27:04.500
Is there any way that I could, uh,
use your phone?

27:05.791 --> 27:08.135
- We don't have no phone, mister.
- Oh.

27:08.227 --> 27:09.604
- That's too bad.
- Yeah.

27:09.828 --> 27:11.637
- Uh...
- No, I said!

27:11.730 --> 27:14.142
Stop it over there, or I'll kick you.

27:14.233 --> 27:16.235
Could I trouble you
for a glass of water?

27:20.339 --> 27:22.979
The water around here
is not really good.

27:23.075 --> 27:25.919
Sit, I said! Stop it! I'm gonna kick you!

27:25.978 --> 27:27.958
Where's Billy Childress?

27:28.747 --> 27:30.522
- Old Bill'?
- Yeah.

27:31.150 --> 27:32.857
He's in his house, mister.

27:33.585 --> 27:34.586
Oh.

27:34.653 --> 27:36.189
This isn't his?

27:37.356 --> 27:41.361
Where... Who do you, uh, live here with?

27:42.127 --> 27:44.164
I think you should go now.

27:44.530 --> 27:45.941
Mmm-hmm. Uh...

27:46.832 --> 27:48.209
Where is he?

27:49.501 --> 27:51.003
All around us.

27:52.204 --> 27:53.877
Before you were born,

27:55.040 --> 27:56.781
and after you die.

27:58.210 --> 28:02.283
No! No! Get out of my house, mister!

28:12.124 --> 28:13.899
Many, clear the house.

28:47.359 --> 28:49.999
Don't move! On your knees, now!

28:51.496 --> 28:53.373
On your knees, now!

28:54.032 --> 28:55.067
No.

30:08.674 --> 30:09.812
Ugh.

30:29.027 --> 30:30.938
Everybody has a phone.

30:31.196 --> 30:32.675
Where's yours?

30:34.366 --> 30:36.346
He's gonna come for you.

30:37.536 --> 30:39.516
He's worse than anybody.

30:41.273 --> 30:42.308
No!

30:42.374 --> 30:44.513
Where's your fucking phone?

30:53.685 --> 30:55.565
Come with me, little man.

30:56.621 --> 30:58.965
Come in here with me.

31:44.603 --> 31:45.707
Rust?

31:47.072 --> 31:48.176
Yeah?

31:48.740 --> 31:50.185
- Rust!
- Here!

32:18.737 --> 32:21.377
Come on inside, little priest.

33:34.012 --> 33:36.151
To your right, little priest.

33:38.884 --> 33:41.296
Take the bride's path.

33:46.858 --> 33:48.633
This is Carcosa.

33:53.231 --> 33:55.472
You know what they did to me?

33:56.368 --> 33:57.813
Hmm?

33:59.004 --> 34:03.009
What I will do
to all the sons and daughters of man.

34:04.409 --> 34:06.218
You blessed, Reggie,

34:07.479 --> 34:08.753
Dewall,

34:10.982 --> 34:12.256
acolytes,

34:14.219 --> 34:16.392
witnesses to my journey.

34:22.727 --> 34:23.933
Lovers.

34:25.363 --> 34:27.343
I'm not ashamed.

34:31.570 --> 34:34.517
Come die with me, little priest.

35:12.143 --> 35:13.247
Rust?

35:24.155 --> 35:25.259
Rust?

37:06.057 --> 37:08.663
Now, take off your mask!

38:39.317 --> 38:40.421
Rust?

39:01.806 --> 39:03.149
Ah!

39:04.475 --> 39:05.613
Oh, fuck!

39:06.644 --> 39:08.885
Ah, he out me pretty good' Marty.

39:09.614 --> 39:10.991
No, Rust.

39:12.851 --> 39:14.330
It ain't bad.

39:15.787 --> 39:17.289
It ain't bad.

39:38.810 --> 39:40.983
Give me a forward team in the house.

39:41.045 --> 39:43.184
Give me a second team on that back house.

39:43.248 --> 39:45.819
Deputy, light up these woods.

40:01.165 --> 40:02.269
Here!

40:04.535 --> 40:06.446
Here! We're here!

40:09.207 --> 40:10.345
Hey!

40:19.284 --> 40:21.628
That's the last thing I remember.

40:21.953 --> 40:23.762
I was on the ground,

40:24.389 --> 40:25.697
sirens.

40:27.759 --> 40:29.739
Saying my friend's name.

40:34.098 --> 40:35.406
The girl is a nut.

40:35.900 --> 40:37.277
She talked some but...

40:37.368 --> 40:40.542
It was a group of guys,
pedophiles and so'f.

40:40.605 --> 40:42.607
Voodoo worship.

40:42.707 --> 40:45.210
The man Cohle shot dead
was the old man's son.

40:45.276 --> 40:46.778
No records.

40:46.878 --> 40:49.051
The girl was at least a half-sister.

40:49.113 --> 40:50.615
- DNA comparison...
- Stop.

40:50.715 --> 40:54.288
Really, man, stop. I don't wanna hear it.

40:55.219 --> 40:58.166
Well, we're still
cataloging everything.

40:58.790 --> 41:01.498
But knife cast came back from that shed.

41:01.793 --> 41:04.000
One of them matched our Lake Charles case.

41:04.095 --> 41:06.575
Another matched Dora Lange's wounds.

41:06.631 --> 41:08.167
Had his prints.

41:09.901 --> 41:12.404
Look, man, we owe you on this collar.

41:13.104 --> 41:14.481
How's Rust?

41:19.744 --> 41:21.246
He hasn't woke up.

41:21.679 --> 41:23.920
Been in a coma since surgery.

41:26.951 --> 41:29.488
They came by when you first got here.

41:34.759 --> 41:37.103
- Ma'am.
- Hi.

41:41.933 --> 41:44.106
It's so good to see you all.

41:45.703 --> 41:47.114
I didn't expect you.

41:57.048 --> 41:58.356
How are you?

42:00.852 --> 42:01.853
Oh...

42:01.953 --> 42:03.227
Good.

42:04.655 --> 42:06.362
I'm fine.

42:10.962 --> 42:13.806
Yeah, I'll be fine. I mean...

42:15.800 --> 42:16.870
lam

42:18.503 --> 42:19.675
fine.

42:37.021 --> 42:38.591
And now, the latest news update

42:38.689 --> 42:40.896
in the case of alleged
Louisiana serial murderer

42:40.992 --> 42:42.835
Errol William Childress.

42:42.894 --> 42:45.431
It's a story that first broke nationwide
two weeks ago,

42:45.530 --> 42:48.534
when two former police officers,
now private detectives,

42:48.599 --> 42:52.570
released information to a number of
news and Jaw enforcement agencies.

42:52.670 --> 42:56.516
Our fast update confirmed
physical evidence at the suspect's home

42:56.574 --> 42:59.214
proved connections
to dozens of missing persons.

43:00.211 --> 43:02.919
In the meantime,
the state attorney general and the FBI

43:03.014 --> 43:04.049
have discredited rumors

43:04.115 --> 43:06.117
that the accused was in some way related

43:06.217 --> 43:09.221
to the family of
Louisiana Senator Edwin 'futile.

44:00.972 --> 44:02.952
What are you doing here?

44:03.574 --> 44:06.077
Nothing. Nurse said I would come in.

44:07.411 --> 44:08.788
Are you watching me sleep?

44:08.846 --> 44:11.452
You know what, I just got here,
I was gonna leave,

44:11.516 --> 44:12.654
but then you woke up.

44:12.750 --> 44:14.491
Jesus, what's your fucking problem?

44:14.585 --> 44:15.996
Nothing. What's your problem?

44:16.087 --> 44:18.931
Not a care in the world.

44:20.625 --> 44:22.263
I saw him, Marty.

44:24.695 --> 44:28.268
He was mowing that school yard
in Pelican Island, in '95.

44:30.701 --> 44:32.305
I couldn't tell how tall he was.

44:33.771 --> 44:37.617
'Cause he was sitting
and his face was dirty, but...

44:38.943 --> 44:40.513
l saw him.

44:43.614 --> 44:45.651
That's what's bugging you?

44:46.651 --> 44:49.131
Turtles... The men in the video...

44:52.957 --> 44:54.959
We didn't get them all.

44:55.026 --> 44:58.166
And we ain't gonna get them all,
that ain't what kind of world it is,

44:58.229 --> 44:59.640
but we got ours.

45:03.334 --> 45:05.473
I'm not supposed to be here.

45:08.406 --> 45:09.885
Yeah, well,

45:11.309 --> 45:13.721
I'll come back by tomorrow, buddy.

45:13.978 --> 45:15.321
Why?

45:16.080 --> 45:17.991
Don't ever change, man.

46:49.573 --> 46:53.146
Doc said, uh,
you'll probably get out in a few days.

46:53.244 --> 46:56.487
I'll make sure you get a
ride, a place to slay.

46:56.580 --> 46:58.582
Yeah, I'll figure it out.

46:59.083 --> 47:01.188
Well, it's already been figured out.

47:01.285 --> 47:02.355
Oh, hey.

47:03.754 --> 47:05.794
I brought you something.

47:10.261 --> 47:11.831
Are we getting engaged?

47:12.363 --> 47:15.936
If we were getting engaged,
I'd have got a nicer ribbon.

47:21.672 --> 47:23.948
- You remembered?
- Yeah.

47:24.809 --> 47:27.289
Ah, let's get out from
under this roof, huh?

47:27.345 --> 47:28.688
Good idea.

47:31.015 --> 47:33.095
Yeah, I can push
two goddamn wheels on my own.

47:33.117 --> 47:37.065
Yeah' I ought to let you
rip out your fucking stitches. Stop it.

47:39.623 --> 47:42.536
Feeling better? You're ahead of me.

47:45.863 --> 47:48.639
Ah, I shouldn't even
fucking be here, Marty.

47:49.533 --> 47:52.480
I believe, "No shit" is the proper response

47:52.536 --> 47:54.038
to that observation.

47:54.972 --> 47:57.043
No, I don't mean like that.

47:57.475 --> 47:59.250
It's something else.

48:00.244 --> 48:02.019
What is so...

48:02.079 --> 48:03.649
Talk to me, Rust.

48:12.022 --> 48:13.763
There was a moment...

48:14.325 --> 48:17.670
I know when I was under
in the dark that something...

48:19.163 --> 48:21.234
Whatever I had been reduced to,

48:21.332 --> 48:23.278
not even consciousness,

48:23.367 --> 48:26.678
it was a vague awareness in the dark...

48:27.438 --> 48:28.712
And I could...

48:31.208 --> 48:34.280
I could feel my definitions fading.

48:36.180 --> 48:38.592
And beneath that darkness,

48:38.682 --> 48:41.629
there was another kind, it was deeper,

48:42.753 --> 48:43.857
warm.

48:44.422 --> 48:46.197
Like a substance.

48:48.859 --> 48:50.532
I could feel, man.

48:51.395 --> 48:52.897
And I knew...

48:53.097 --> 48:57.477
I knew my daughter waited for me there.

48:58.536 --> 48:59.640
So clear...

49:00.371 --> 49:02.044
I could feel her.

49:04.375 --> 49:06.048
I could feel them.

49:07.144 --> 49:10.591
I could feel a piece of my pop, too.

49:13.217 --> 49:17.563
It was like I was a part
of everything that I ever loved.

49:17.621 --> 49:19.259
And we were all,

49:20.724 --> 49:23.227
the three of us, just fading out.

49:27.431 --> 49:30.173
And all I had to do was let go.

49:32.436 --> 49:33.779
And I did.

49:35.906 --> 49:38.011
I said, "Darkness, yeah!"

49:40.911 --> 49:42.584
And I disappeared.

49:45.015 --> 49:47.586
But I could still feel

49:49.253 --> 49:50.789
her love there.

49:52.590 --> 49:54.467
Even more than before.

49:56.494 --> 49:57.837
Nothing...

50:02.700 --> 50:04.611
Nothing but that love.

50:17.781 --> 50:19.522
And then I woke up.

50:25.456 --> 50:26.628
Hey, uh...

50:32.696 --> 50:33.697
Didn't, uh...

50:35.299 --> 50:37.905
Didn't you tell me one time, at dinner,

50:38.903 --> 50:41.474
once, maybe, about... You used to...

50:43.807 --> 50:46.253
You used to make up
stories about the stars?

50:48.812 --> 50:51.019
Yeah, I was

50:52.983 --> 50:54.360
in Alaska

50:55.319 --> 50:57.162
under the night skies.

50:57.555 --> 51:00.331
Yeah. You used to lay there and look up.

51:01.158 --> 51:03.001
Yeah. At the stars.

51:05.162 --> 51:10.009
You remember,
I never watched a TV till I was 17,

51:10.067 --> 51:11.910
so there wasn't much to
fucking do out there,

51:12.002 --> 51:14.107
besides walk around, explore.

51:15.005 --> 51:16.006
And...

51:16.774 --> 51:20.221
And then look up at the stars
and make up stories.

51:21.111 --> 51:22.454
Like what?

51:24.348 --> 51:28.023
I'll tell you, Marty,
I've been up in that room,

51:28.085 --> 51:30.463
looking out those windows every night here.

51:30.554 --> 51:32.192
Just thinking

51:38.395 --> 51:40.204
it's just one story.

51:41.532 --> 51:42.909
The oldest.

51:46.870 --> 51:48.247
What's that?

51:50.808 --> 51:52.481
Light versus dark.

51:56.547 --> 51:57.651
Well,

51:58.716 --> 52:00.923
I know we ain't in Alaska

52:02.620 --> 52:06.568
but it appears to me
that the dark has a lot more territory.

52:10.961 --> 52:12.065
Yeah.

52:13.564 --> 52:15.510
You're right about that.

52:21.171 --> 52:23.173
- Hey, listen. Hey.
- Yeah, what?

52:23.907 --> 52:26.581
Could you point me
in the direction of that car?

52:26.644 --> 52:30.456
Man, I spent enough of my fucking life
in a hospital.

52:31.482 --> 52:33.325
Jesus. Oh!

52:33.417 --> 52:36.125
You know what? I'd protest

52:36.954 --> 52:39.935
but it occurs to me that
you're un-killable.

52:40.491 --> 52:42.994
You wanna go back,
get your clothes or anything?

52:43.093 --> 52:46.040
No. Anything I left back
there, I don't need.

52:51.935 --> 52:54.006
You're looking at it wrong,

52:54.538 --> 52:56.449
at the sky.

52:57.374 --> 52:58.785
How's that?

53:00.511 --> 53:02.388
Once there was only dark.

53:05.115 --> 53:07.891
If you ask me, the light's winning.
